Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 23:31:06 +0200
Subject: loginDialog: Close auth menu before selecting the active mechanism
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The mechanism selection synchronously triggers a mechanisms-changed
signal that rebuilds (and disposes) the items, so we must deactivate /
close the menu while the items are still alive, otherwise
PopupMenuBase._activeMenuItem ends up pointing at a disposed object.

    (gnome-shell:1769639): Gjs-CRITICAL **: 23:28:15.033: Object
    Gjs_gdm_authMenuButton_AuthMenuItem (0x5a6aaaa886f0), has been
    already disposed — impossible to access it.
    This might be caused by the object having been destroyed from C code
    using something such as destroy(), dispose(), or remove() vfuncs.
